%description:

Tcp.tcpAlgorithmClass:qualified-alias -- a qualified NED type name selects that type.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "a type of the package inet.transportlayer.tcp.flavours, or a qualified
NED type name".

The classes: the nine algorithms of the package inet.transportlayer.tcp.flavours (TcpNewReno is
the default, TcpReno the value of LegacyTcp, TcpCubic of LinuxTcp), qualified-alias (a
qualified NED type name), unknown (a name without a NED type: an error) and socket-override
(the open command of a socket selects another algorithm). Each test of an algorithm checks a
behavior that none of the other eight algorithms shows. The code:
TcpConnection::createTcpAlgorithm() and the classes of the algorithms. A qualified name is another spelling of a short name, so the test passes with "TcpReno" by
design, and the cross-class check skips it.

Host under test: host1. Observation: level 3, the algorithm of the connection of host1 is
inet::tcp::TcpReno when its SYN goes; the wire cannot show the name of a type.

%# parameter: Tcp.tcpAlgorithmClass
%# class: qualified-alias
%# value: "inet.transportlayer.tcp.flavours.TcpReno"
%# key: *.host1.tcp.tcpAlgorithmClass
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpAlgorithmClassQualifiedAlias")
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
             .first()
                  .assertModule("host1.tcp.conn-*", "tcpAlgorithm.className == \"inet::tcp::TcpReno\"")
             .describe("the SYN of host1")
             .within(0.5));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpAlgorithmClassQualifiedAlias compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.tcpAlgorithmClass = "inet.transportlayer.tcp.flavours.TcpReno"    # the parameter under test
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpAlgorithmClassQualifiedAlias: PASS
